WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.901
-Our next guest

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:04.070
is an Oscar-, Emmy-,
and Grammy-winning artist

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.738
who has a new album called

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.374
"A Beautiful Revolution:
Part 2."

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.176
This comes out September 10th.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.712
Ladies and gentlemen,
here is Common.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.681
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.482
-♪ There's Brother Common ♪

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.752
♪ Any fool can see ♪

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.286
♪ He's in his finest ♪

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.855
♪ It's 'cause of Tiffany ♪

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.657
♪ His brand-new album ♪

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.893
♪ Beautiful and wise ♪

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.896
♪ His revolution,
it will be televised ♪

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:35.801
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.604
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.538
-Man, so great to be here.
-You're a stud, buddy.

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:41.341
Thanks for always --
Every time you come,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.809
we always ask you
to do something crazy,

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.010
and you're like, "I'm up.
Let's try it."

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.046
-To me, it's just like,
I love having fun,

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.648
and I don't take myself
as serious as people think.

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:50.850
So you gotta have fun, man.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.952
-You gotta kick it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.320
-Yeah. They love you.
That's why they love you.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.322
-Yeah.
-I want to talk about

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.658
the new record, by the way,
the new album.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.526
Who did the art on this?

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.695
-It's an artist by the name
Derrick Boateng.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:06.132
He's from Ghana.
And he takes pictures

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.368
all around his environment,

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.603
and he takes
these beautiful pictures

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:14.874
of Black people in Ghana,
and he gives the proceeds

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.809
to the communities
that he takes it from.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.011
-Oh, I love it.
-Thank you.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.578
-It's a great --
It's a great cover.

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:21.581
"A Beautiful Revolution:
Part 2."

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.949
-Yeah.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.917
-I can't believe that you get
a little nervous.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:28.021
I mean, you just performed for
President Obama's at his 60th.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.224
-Yeah, I was more nervous
to do the rap remix

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.360
than to do President Obama's --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.161
-Do you get nervous, though,
before, if you're performing

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:38.597
in front of -- I mean,
there's some big names there.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.500
-I mean, I get a little nervous,
but it's those good nerves.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.437
And then, you know --
I was performing with my family,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.607
with The Roots and Erykah Badu,
so it was just like --

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.642
it was home for us.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.810
-You know, I wanted --
I wanted the President

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.913
to enjoy his birthday
and just give the music

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:57.183
and do the things we love,
so it was more fun.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.851
I like being
a little nervous, though.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.320
-Do you get --
Did you get him a gift?

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.157
-You know -- I didn't --
I didn't get him a gift, man.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.291
It was like --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.493
I was --
You know, the Secret Service

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.696
check everything anyway.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.866
And then, too, I was like,
man, you know, my gift --

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.034
my gift was --
-What do you get him?

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.902
-I just brought my talent
to the table.

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:19.371
-Yeah, exactly.
That's exactly --

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.073
See, that's exactly right.
You know what?

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:23.509
That is a gift.
-No, no, but seriously.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:24.877
I thought about it later, like,

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.145
"Damn, I didn't
get him anything."

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.313
But what do you get
the president?

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.682
-Oh, I have no clue.
But isn't it true that --

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.384
Didn't he -- Doesn't he owe
you a birthday gift?

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:36.322
-Yeah. You know what?
My mother, actually, is really

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.892
great friends with someone
that works for the President.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.227
And for one of my birthdays,
she got me the gift that I was

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.530
supposed to play President Obama
in a one-on-one in basketball.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.267
It was years ago, and I never
got to fulfill that prophecy.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:51.470
-But you love basketball.
I mean, yeah, you're a player.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.639
-I love basketball.
I was ready to play him,

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:56.009
and I was ready to beat him,
no matter what.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.177
[ Laughter ]
And, like, it wasn't --

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:00.680
I wasn't gonna back down
because he was the president.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.514
-No.
-Or Secret Service is around

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:03.816
doing their thing.
-Yeah, some people do that.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:04.917
Yeah, yeah.
They go like, "Oh, he just --

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.386
Yeah, he scored,
you know, 89 points."

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.388
[ Laughter ]
"Wow, he's really getting you."

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:10.956
No, you would play --
-No, I was gonna go hard.

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:12.391
I know it.
I got love for Michelle,

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:13.626
I got love for the family,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.062
but I wanted to beat
Barack Obama.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.997
You know what?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:20.099
-And you never --
Well, you can still do it now.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.634
You can do it now.
-Yeah, I don't know

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.337
if he's playing, like,
straight up games.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.006
He probably would want to play
golf, but I could play horse.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.874
You know, horse.
-How is our pal?

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.043
How is Tiffany Haddish?
How's Tiffany doing?

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.477
-Aw, she's super good, man.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.580
Tiffany's out
changing the world, man.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.583
She like -- You know, she's
always doing something really,

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:39.852
like, creative or trying to do
something for the community

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.954
or buying land.
She loves those things.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.089
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, really?

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.590
-Yes.
-She's so interesting.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.158
I think she's fascinating.
-She is very interesting.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.994
-Not only is she gorgeous,
but she's funny and smart.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.329
I just love having her
as a guest.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.964
Please give her our best.
-I will.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.433
I will definitely send love.
[ Applause ]

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:57.703
-You were friends
before you started dating.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:00.272
-Yeah.
-Who asked who out?

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:03.609
-Well, really wasn't, like,
an official ask, meaning like --

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.277
You know, we weren't like...
-Yeah.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.513
-...in elementary school
like I handed her a note, like,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.781
"Will you go with me?"
-Circle yes.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.983
-"Circle yes" --
I didn't do that.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:12.284
[ Laughter ]
But after being friends

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:15.421
and hanging out,
it was just one good night,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.857
cool night where we had
a couple drinks and...

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.326
[ Laughter ]
...and a little twinkle

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.961
in the eye, and I was just like,
"Oh, actually,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.397
I think she might like me."
'Cause I had been trying,

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:27.200
and she would put me in
the friend boat for a second.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.267
And I was cool
with the friend boat.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.635
I was like, "We friends."
-Okay.

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:31.404
-Yeah, but you know,
like you was saying,

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:34.207
you've been in that experience.
-Yeah, my wife, yeah.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.175
She's still -- yeah.
That's how we --

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.676
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:38.844
-You're not
in the friend boat no more.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:40.546
-No, not in
the friend boat anymore.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.514
But, yeah.
But we started

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:44.317
in the friend boat
'cause we were just hanging out,

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.653
and I would, like,
have these parties

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:49.522
in my hotel room with the crew
and everybody, and I'd D.J.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.358
And by the end of the night,
she would be the only one left

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.160
because I'm not a great D.J.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.463
But I go, "She likes me."

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.332
And so, we just hung out
and were just friends,

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:01.300
and that was it.
And then, we were --

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.502
She produced this movie,
and we're selling the movie,

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.104
and I saw her, and I go,
"I miss you."

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.371
She goes, "I miss you, too."
-Ah, man.

00:05:06.371 --> 00:05:07.439
-"We should hang out."

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:08.740
And then,
we've been married 16 years.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.310
-16 years.
That's love, man.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.445
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love that.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:13.712
-But that's the best way
to do it.

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:14.947
-That's the best way.
-Just go,

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.015
"Let's just being friends,
having a good time."

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.816
-Just be friends, right.
-I love it.

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:21.019
I want to talk about this now.
September 10th, this comes out.

00:05:21.019 --> 00:05:23.789
"A Beautiful Revolution:
Part 2."

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.224
What's the inspiration?
Did you always know

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.493
there was gonna to be number two
when you did the first one?

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.961
-The first one?
Yeah.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.996
I kind of -- when I was
in the studio, I was like,

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:33.699
"Man, it would be nice
to continue this energy

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.601
of what we were creating."

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.304
And "Part 1" was a little more,
like, intense

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.671
and had the revolution there,
because it was

00:05:39.671 --> 00:05:41.840
the political climate
that was going on in the fall.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.542
-Yeah.
-But this one is more about,

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.713
like, bringing inspiration
and joy in a different way

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:50.583
and, like, hope and optimism.
So, I wanted the music to, like,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.351
be uplifting, and you feel good,

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:54.920
but also get some
good food for your soul.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.321
So that's what this album is,

00:05:56.321 --> 00:05:59.257
and we took it
a lot of different places.

00:05:59.257 --> 00:06:01.994
But I feel like the music is,
like, about rejoicing.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.062
-Wait till you guys hear this

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.163
and see this
performance tonight.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.032
"When We Move" is the song.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:10.403
-And it is so good.
And you were saying --

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.638
Well, I mean, you know
Black Thought for how long now?

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.440
The Roots?
-Let me tell you,

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.610
I wouldn't be sitting
on this couch right here

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.412
if it weren't for The Roots,
to be honest.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:22.581
Like, that's my family.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:28.453
And...
I first -- I love The Roots.

00:06:28.453 --> 00:06:30.923
I love their music.
But when I first saw them,

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.125
Ahmir remember this story.
They were performing

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.527
at this place in Chicago
called The Double Door,

00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:37.530
and I was, like,
talking to this girl,

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.931
kind of really loving the show

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.399
but trying to ignore her
and trying to be cool.

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.068
I was just being an asswipe.
I don't know why.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.135
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:45.571
But then,
I got to talk to them,

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.039
and I was like,
"Man, these dudes are cool.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.507
I love they music."

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:51.310
And then, man, from that point,
we started working together.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.046
I went to Philly.
Tariq let me stay at his crib.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:57.216
He introduced me to Fela Kuti.
He was cooking good fish.

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:59.251
I heard y'all
had cook-offs, too.

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:02.255
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Cooking good fish.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:04.657
Yo, when I saw them
win a Grammy, I was like,

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:06.225
"Damn, I could win a Grammy."

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.793
Like, 'cause it's just
my family doing this.

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:09.261
-Right.
-So, this is --

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:10.830
This is family, man.
When I see them --

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.032
We've known each other
over 20 years, so...

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:15.934
-Yeah. Well, I love it
when you come on the show.

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.069
And we obviously love it
when you come on the show.

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.270
Hopefully, this feels
like home to you.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.872
-This is home, man.
-I love you, buddy.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.541
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

